Build a working qPCR analysis application in this new repository.

PRODUCT GOAL

Create a browser-based research workbench for laboratory colleagues who
do not program. They must be able to upload qPCR results, confirm samples
and plate layouts, inspect measurement quality, calculate expression
changes, compare experiments, and export meeting/publication figures.

The main use case is screening small activating RNA (saRNA) designs.
Also support time-course, culture-condition, reference-gene evaluation,
storage/handling, and assay-reproducibility experiments.

Deliver functioning software with persistent storage and verified
calculations—not just a dashboard mockup.

WORKING APPROACH

Inspect repository instructions and available example files first.
Write a concise implementation plan, then implement it.

Make routine implementation decisions autonomously. Ask questions only
when missing information affects scientific correctness or interpretation.
Continue independent work while questions remain unresolved.

Do not silently invent sample identities, biological independence,
control assignments, or plate boundaries.

Keep unresolved imported data editable and prevent affected calculations
from appearing complete.

Do not deploy publicly unless requested.

ARCHITECTURE

Use:
- Python for the scientific engine and import processing.
- FastAPI with Pydantic for the service boundary.
- SQLite for initial persistent storage.
- React with TypeScript and Vite for the browser